<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pacta conventa (Croatia)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1102</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pacta conventa is a document that claims to record an agreement of about 1102 between King Coloman of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and twelve Croatian noble families, guaranteeing their lands and freedoms in return for accepting him as king. It survives only in a 14th-century copy, and most historians consider it a later forgery or reconstruction, though it reflects the real autonomy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> kept in its union with Hungary.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pacta-conventa-croatia.jpg" alt="Pacta conventa (Croatia)" width="320" height="551" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pacta_Conventa_(Croatia).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
